WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:07.460
If we are given this image and asked what

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:10.290
exactly this is, I am sure your answer will

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:12.110
be a “Cell”!

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:15.140
Now to study this, we need to study every

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:17.480
component present within.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:20.000
And not only within, we even need to study

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.600
the covering that is this part in detail.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:27.120
Can you tell me, what exactly is this named as?

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:28.590
That’s right!

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:31.680
It is called the cell membrane or the plasma membrane.

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:35.020
In our previous video we have learned that

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:37.340
the cell membrane is selectively permeable

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:39.170
in nature.

00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:42.240
That is, it only allows specific materials

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:45.060
to enter and leave the cell.

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:47.540
Any guesses what is the plasma membrane made

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:48.060
up of?

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:51.340
The plasma membrane is made up of lipids and

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:54.820
proteins and also has some carbohydrate chains.

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:57.720
There are two things that freely move in and

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:58.580
out of the cell.

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:01.820
Those include Gases and Water!

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:04.980
Do you think these molecules need energy for

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:06.860
travelling across the membrane?

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:10.080
Let us take a simple example to understand

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:12.680
what exactly happens in this case.

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:15.660
We know what happens when a drop of ink is

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:17.400
added to a glass of water.

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:20.780
The single dark colored ink drop spreads when

00:01:20.782 --> 00:01:23.380
added to water and the intense blue color

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:25.170
fades slightly.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:27.583
If we see at the molecular level, then the

00:01:27.583 --> 00:01:29.939
ink molecules, which are compactly packed

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:32.980
in the single drop get a chance of dispersing

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:36.280
in a larger area when added to the water.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:38.940
This is nothing but the process of Diffusion.

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:42.780
And we know that this dispersal process does

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:44.060
not require energy.

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:47.194
The molecules just try to move freely in the

00:01:47.194 --> 00:01:49.690
space available and as a result, diffusion

00:01:49.690 --> 00:01:50.680
occurs!

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:54.514
The same story is seen when gas or water molecules

00:01:54.514 --> 00:01:56.579
travel across the membrane!

00:01:56.579 --> 00:01:59.840
Take carbon dioxide for example.

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:02.747
When cells undergo cellular respiration, a

00:02:02.747 --> 00:02:06.000
lot of carbon dioxide accumulates in the cells.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.260
On the other hand, there is a very little

00:02:08.260 --> 00:02:11.080
carbon dioxide present outside the cells.

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:14.370
Hence the carbon dioxide molecules move outside

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:15.560
the cells.

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:18.920
Now, there is very little oxygen left after

00:02:18.921 --> 00:02:20.870
respiration in the cells.

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:23.365
So the oxygen from outside the cells moves

00:02:23.365 --> 00:02:25.800
in through the plasma membrane to make up

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:27.480
for the lost oxygen.

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:31.340
That means Carbon dioxide moves OUT and oxygen

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:32.800
moves IN!

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:36.000
Both the gases move from their area of higher

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:39.100
concentration to an area of lower concentration.

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:43.720
And this diffusion process does not require energy.

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:46.651
Diffusion is one of the processes by which

00:02:46.651 --> 00:02:49.930
transportation of several substances is carried

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:52.220
out across the cell membrane.

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:55.580
But it is not the only one process on which

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:56.640
the cell relies.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:59.218
There are a few more methods that the cell

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:01.780
adopts for transportation of substances.

00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:06.640
Let us have a look at these processes in the next video!

